WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.180 --> 00:00:01.860
- All right, let's wrap up this hour with

00:00:01.860 --> 00:00:03.480
something cool I found on social media.

00:00:03.480 --> 00:00:04.712
This is, "What I'm Liking"

00:00:04.712 --> 00:00:07.260
(upbeat music)
(audience applauding)

00:00:07.260 --> 00:00:09.930
It's impressive to see
even one person leaping

00:00:09.930 --> 00:00:12.030
out of a perfectly good airplane.

00:00:12.030 --> 00:00:13.590
But check out this view.

00:00:13.590 --> 00:00:15.870
Yep, that's 80 women who came together

00:00:15.870 --> 00:00:17.610
for a Guinness World record breaking

00:00:17.610 --> 00:00:20.880
vertical skydive over the Arizona desert

00:00:20.880 --> 00:00:22.200
and it was all for a purpose.

00:00:22.200 --> 00:00:24.330
We have the co-captain
and one of the sky divers

00:00:24.330 --> 00:00:26.820
of Project 19 on the line to explain.

00:00:26.820 --> 00:00:30.000
Let's say hi to Amy watching
on Arizona's family.

00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:32.980
What's up Amy? (audience applauding)

00:00:32.980 --> 00:00:36.240
- Hi, Kelly. Thank you for having me.

00:00:36.240 --> 00:00:37.350
- Oh my God, absolutely.

00:00:37.350 --> 00:00:38.910
So before we talk about the why,

00:00:38.910 --> 00:00:42.000
explain to me the how, 80
women did that at once.

00:00:42.000 --> 00:00:42.833
- The how.

00:00:42.833 --> 00:00:46.740
So there were about 120 women,

00:00:46.740 --> 00:00:49.710
some of the best sky divers
from all over the world.

00:00:49.710 --> 00:00:52.410
There were 22 countries represented.

00:00:52.410 --> 00:00:54.840
And at first we trained in small groups

00:00:54.840 --> 00:00:55.980
all over the world.

00:00:55.980 --> 00:00:59.070
And then we came together
in one big group.

00:00:59.070 --> 00:01:01.500
- [Kelly] Look at that, oh my gosh.

00:01:01.500 --> 00:01:03.300
Well, this jump like many with

00:01:03.300 --> 00:01:05.790
Project 19 had a purpose, right?

00:01:05.790 --> 00:01:08.550
- Yes, this jump was so special

00:01:08.550 --> 00:01:10.710
because it was inspired

00:01:10.710 --> 00:01:13.560
by the women of the suffrage movement.

00:01:13.560 --> 00:01:18.560
In 1920, women got the right
to vote in the United States

00:01:18.690 --> 00:01:21.270
and as professional female skydivers

00:01:21.270 --> 00:01:24.420
we wanted to do something bold and brave

00:01:24.420 --> 00:01:28.080
like these women and to honor these women.

00:01:28.080 --> 00:01:31.800
So we kind of came up with
this idea and implemented it

00:01:31.800 --> 00:01:34.860
to do this record in honor of them.

00:01:34.860 --> 00:01:37.020
And, yeah, we'd been working on it

00:01:37.020 --> 00:01:40.950
for a really long time
and just so excited.

00:01:40.950 --> 00:01:44.670
Women in skydiving only represent

00:01:44.670 --> 00:01:49.320
14% of all of active skydivers
in the United States.

00:01:49.320 --> 00:01:52.230
So we really wanted to change that.

00:01:52.230 --> 00:01:54.930
We're on a mission to change that.

00:01:54.930 --> 00:01:57.690
And we actually have
another record planned

00:01:57.690 --> 00:01:59.730
in about a year from now.

00:01:59.730 --> 00:02:01.050
We're gonna do another world record

00:02:01.050 --> 00:02:04.140
but it's gonna be both men
and women working together.

00:02:04.140 --> 00:02:07.350
But, the fun thing is that it's gonna be

00:02:07.350 --> 00:02:10.770
only women in the leadership role.

00:02:10.770 --> 00:02:12.180
- Oh, wow.

00:02:12.180 --> 00:02:15.120
It's so amazing what y'all
create (audience applauding)

00:02:15.120 --> 00:02:17.190
like the art in the sky.

00:02:17.190 --> 00:02:19.410
It looks like Tony's
Stark has just released

00:02:19.410 --> 00:02:22.470
all his things at once. It's incredible.

00:02:22.470 --> 00:02:23.850
Thank you so much, Amy.

00:02:23.850 --> 00:02:25.020
I'm liking your post right now.

00:02:25.020 --> 00:02:26.177
You are one brave woman.

00:02:26.177 --> 00:02:28.230
(bell dinging and audience clapping)

00:02:28.230 --> 00:02:29.670
and that's not all.
- [Amy] Thank you, Kelly.

00:02:29.670 --> 00:02:30.503
- That's not all.

00:02:30.503 --> 00:02:32.760
Our season long partner,
Pilot Pin, makers of G2,

00:02:32.760 --> 00:02:34.290
the go-to pin of "The
Kelly Clarkson Show,"

00:02:34.290 --> 00:02:36.431
want to honor truly unstoppable people

00:02:36.431 --> 00:02:39.390
apparently just like
you and your colleagues

00:02:39.390 --> 00:02:41.280
so they're gonna be writing you a check

00:02:41.280 --> 00:02:43.860
to the Women's Skydiving
Network for a thousand dollars.

00:02:43.860 --> 00:02:46.231
How's that sound?
(audience applauding)

00:02:46.231 --> 00:02:49.020
- Oh, Kelly, thank you so much.

00:02:49.020 --> 00:02:51.390
Thank you for all the good work you do.

00:02:51.390 --> 00:02:52.223
- Oh, absolutely.

00:02:52.223 --> 00:02:53.220
Have a great day, Amy

00:02:53.220 --> 00:02:55.650
and thank you so much
to all our guests today,

00:02:55.650 --> 00:02:57.150
Vin Diesel, Quentin Plair, and Noah.

00:02:57.150 --> 00:02:57.983
Y'all have a great night.

00:02:57.983 --> 00:02:59.650
And if it's not, try and change it.

